WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
The people I grew up with—we all know this.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.700
But when I talk to people on the internet, like my friends in the North, they don’t.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.520
They can’t process it when I tell them, “No. I was segregated.

4
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.500
I wasn’t allowed to do this.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.140
And no, I wasn’t allowed to sit here.”

6
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:19.510
And to them, they can’t process because we are the exact same age, and they can’t see that blacks and whites grew up like that.

7
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.020
We still had to use the back door in the nineties when I was little.

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.260
So, it’s one of those . . . it’s hard trying to explain to them, and they’re like, “What?”

9
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:32.280
And me, I don’t understand how they didn’t experience that, because we all . . . all me and my friends experienced that.

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.600
So why didn’t y’all experience that?

11
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.300
So, it’s one of those . . . it’s like a culture shock,

12
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.320
because you’re telling me you didn’t go through it, and I’m telling you that I went through it.
